 Where:
-- $T_{\text{scan}}(\sigma, N) = \frac{N}{64} \cdot t_{\text{word}}$ is the bitset traversal cost (dominated by `u64` iteration and trailing-zeros extraction).
-- $t_{\text{dist}}(d)$ is the latency of computing distance over $d$ float dimensions via 8-way unrolled kernel. On Intel Core i7-12650H:
-  $$t_{\text{dist}}(128) \approx 4.2 \text{ ns}$$
-- $t_{\text{heap}}(k)$ is the amortized cost of maintaining a max-heap of size $k=10$:
-  $$t_{\text{heap}}(10) \approx 0.8 \text{ ns}$$
-Thus, for SIFT1M ($d=128$), the per-vector scan evaluation cost is:
-$$t_{\text{cand}} \approx 5.0 \text{ ns/vector}$$
+- $T_{\text{scan}}(N) = \frac{N}{64} \cdot t_{\text{word}}$ is the bitset traversal cost.
+- $t_{\text{cand}} = t_{\text{dist}}(d) + t_{\text{heap}}(k)$ is the per-matching-vector cost (distance kernel plus heap update).
+- $t_{\text{word}}$, $t_{\text{dist}}$, $t_{\text{heap}}$ come from a single-threaded microbenchmark on the target machine (pinned core, Phase 4 protocol).
 
 #### Cost Model: In-Traversal Graph Traversal ($C_{\text{graph}}$)
-The cost of Strategy 2 comprises greedy entry zoom-in plus Layer 0 beam exploration:
-$$C_{\text{graph}}(\sigma, ef) = L_{\text{zoom}} \cdot t_{\text{hop}} + N_{\text{eval}}(\sigma, ef) \cdot \left[ t_{\text{dist}}(d) + t_{\text{mem\_lat}} \right] + N_{\text{visited}} \cdot t_{\text{pred}}$$
-Where:
-- $N_{\text{eval}}(\sigma, ef)$ is the number of distance evaluations performed during graph search. When selectivity is $\sigma$, the search must expand more candidates to satisfy $ef$ matching items:
-  $$N_{\text{eval}}(\sigma, ef) \approx ef \cdot M \cdot \left( \frac{1}{\sigma^\beta} \right)$$
-  where $\beta \approx 0.35 - 0.50$ represents the topological dilation factor of navigating through non-matching bridge vertices.
-- $t_{\text{mem\_lat}}$ is the memory latency penalty. Because graph neighbors are stored in non-contiguous arena allocations, each edge traversal incurs a high L3 cache miss probability:
-  $$t_{\text{mem\_lat}} \approx 35 \text{ ns}$$
-- Total effective time per graph evaluation:
-  $$t_{\text{graph\_cand}} \approx t_{\text{dist}}(128) + t_{\text{mem\_lat}} \approx 4.2 + 35.0 = 39.2 \text{ ns/eval}$$
+$$C_{\text{graph}}(\sigma, ef) = N_{\text{eval}}(\sigma, ef) \cdot t_{\text{graph\_cand}} + N_{\text{visited}} \cdot t_{\text{pred}} + C_{\text{zoom}}$$
+$$N_{\text{eval}}(\sigma, ef) \approx ef \cdot M \cdot \sigma^{-\beta}$$
+Where $\beta$ is a fitted dilation exponent (the power-law form is a modelling assumption, checked with a goodness-of-fit report against the measured distance-evaluation counters) and $t_{\text{graph\_cand}}$ is the measured per-evaluation cost including cache misses (measured $C_{\text{graph}}$ divided by the measured evaluation count).
 
