-### 4.2 Derivation of Theoretical Crossover Selectivity $\sigma^*$
-The crossover selectivity threshold $\sigma^*$ is defined as the exact selectivity where pre-filter brute force matches graph traversal latency:
-$$C_{\text{brute}}(\sigma^*, N, d) = C_{\text{graph}}(\sigma^*, ef)$$
-
-Equating the two formulations:
-$$\sigma^* N \cdot t_{\text{cand}} = N_{\text{eval}}(\sigma^*, ef) \cdot t_{\text{graph\_cand}}$$
-
-$$\sigma^* \cdot N \cdot t_{\text{cand}} \approx ef \cdot M \cdot \left( \frac{1}{(\sigma^*)^\beta} \right) \cdot t_{\text{graph\_cand}}$$
-
-Multiplying by $(\sigma^*)^\beta$:
-$$(\sigma^*)^{1 + \beta} \approx \frac{ef \cdot M}{N} \cdot \left( \frac{t_{\text{graph\_cand}}}{t_{\text{cand}}} \right)$$
-
-$$\boxed{\sigma^*(N) \approx \left[ \frac{ef \cdot M}{N} \cdot \left( \frac{t_{\text{dist}} + t_{\text{mem\_lat}}}{t_{\text{dist}} + t_{\text{heap}}} \right) \right]^{\frac{1}{1 + \beta}}}$$
